    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §156-a, Exec L (as proposed in S.8742 & A.9337)",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S736\n\nSPONSOR: CLEARE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to hazardous materials\nemergency response training for incidents involving lithium-ion\nbatteries\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment to L.2024, c.199, to make technical changes\nfor clarity and consistency with similar laws regarding lithium-ion\nbatteries.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by modifying the\nprovisions to appropriately reference section 495 of the general busi-\nness law in regards to the definition of lithium-ion battery.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 199 of the Laws of 2024. 5.8742 and A.9337,\nboth passed the Senate and Assembly, respectfully, in March and May\n2024.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2024 amending the executive law, in relation to\nhazardous materials emergency response training for incidents involving\nlithium-ion batteries, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S.8742\nand A.9337, takes effect.\n",
